# caught-looking

- **Stack**: Go 1.26 API (`backend/`, chi), React 19 + Vite + TypeScript (`frontend/`).
- **Local dev**: from repo root, `make dev` runs the API (:8080) and Vite; the frontend proxies `/api` to the backend (see `Makefile`).
- **Scoped rules**: follow the matching `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` when editing frontend TSX/hooks, API client/types, OpenAPI, tests, backend Go, or **`README.md`**. Frontend Prettier: **`frontend-prettier`** (run Prettier on changed files). Editor format-on-save: **`.vscode/settings.json`**.
- **Workflow skills** (read `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` when the task fits):
  - **`openapi-maintain`** / **`add-api-endpoint`** — API contract and new routes
  - **`backend-go-tests`** / **`frontend-vitest-tests`** — tests
  - **`backend-http-security`** / **`caching-and-upstream-perf`** — hardening and upstream/cache performance
  - **`pr-ready`** — local CI-parity checks before a PR
- **Before opening a PR**: follow **`.cursor/skills/pr-ready/SKILL.md`**. CI must pass (`frontend`: OpenAPI lint + generated-type drift check, lint, Prettier check, typecheck, test, build; `backend`: vet, govulncheck, test, build). For API edits, run **`make check-openapi`**. Fill out `.github/pull_request_template.md`.
